{
  "manufacturer": "Senva",
  "manufacturer_slug": "senva",
  "model": "TG series toxic/combustible gas monitor (RS-485 Modbus)",
  "model_slug": "tg-gas-monitor",
  "short_model": "TG",
  "aliases": [
    "Senva TG",
    "TG series"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (gas detector)",
  "applies_to": "Senva TG series RS-485 gas monitors (one or two gas sensors, optional temperature), Modbus Protocol Guide 154-0036-0A (2020-02-07).",
  "summary": "The Senva TG is a wall-mount gas monitor with one or two gas sensors, a fan relay, an alarm relay and a buzzer, plus an RS-485 port that auto-detects BACnet MS/TP, Modbus RTU or Modbus ASCII. All data is in holding registers. This map covers communication setup, units, setpoints and hysteresis, sensor life and status, system state, relay and buzzer control, and the gas, temperature and supply-voltage readings with their statistics.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "ASCII"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The guide prints raw protocol addresses prefixed with R (R320 = address 320); in Modicon notation that is 40321. 'R320/21' is a 2-register value starting at 320."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "TG Modbus Protocol Guide",
    "doc_number": "154-0036-0A",
    "revision_date": "2020-02-07",
    "url": "https://www.zotsupply.com/content/PDFs/Senva/Gas%20Monitoring/154-0036-0A.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "register index pp. 2-3; configuration p. 5; register details pp. 7-19; data types p. 20"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Source host: the unaltered Senva guide hosted by a distributor; we did not find it on Senva's own site.",
    "Word order: the guide says UINT32 and FLOAT use two registers in full network byte order, MSB first, and gives UINT32 byte examples, so high word first (ABCD).",
    "BOOL registers are listed as UINT16 with 0/1 values. The default slave address is 100 plus the last two digits of the serial number; baud, parity and data bits are auto-detected by default.",
    "Gas concentrations are FLOAT values; the guide gives setpoint defaults in ppm but does not print a unit on the concentration registers.",
    "The source prints inconsistent value codes for R201 (4-8 for sensor 2 status) and R230 (4/5 for the alarm relay), so no value table is given for them.",
    "Left out: User Data R294-301 (free storage) and Sensor calibration registers mentioned but not listed (R156, R166)."
  ],
